JS8Core is an independent implementation of the JS8 protocol. It is
distributed under the MIT license (see LICENSE).

Portions of this distribution include on-air protocol constants, LDPC and
varicode mappings, and the index-ordered JSC dictionary required for
interoperability. The JSC search index and receive FIR are independently
generated. See docs/protocol-data-provenance.md for the per-table inventory.

The classification of protocol data does not itself determine copyright
ownership or establish that a dictionary compilation lacks protected
selection or arrangement. Review third-party rights before release.

